\subsection{Discussion of Findings}

The empirical results validate the robustness of the WM v1.2 architecture:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Cross-Model Convergence:} All major frontier LLMs (DeepSeek, Grok, Gemini) independently converged on a remarkably tight CWI band ($44.1 - 44.9$) and Gunning Fog index ($15.6 - 15.8$) when synthesizing English Trinity essays. This demonstrates that WM v1.2 successfully captures the inherent syntactic signature of synthetic LLM generation.
    \item \textbf{Zero False-Positives on Human Prose:} Pre-AI human historical texts ($32.7$ CWI), multi-lingual drafts, and model-polished human prose consistently scored below $40.0$ CWI, proving that the framework respects genuine human literary variance.
    \item \textbf{Language Normalization Efficacy:} The application of the $\alpha_L = 0.85$ normalization factor successfully accounted for compound-word orthographic mass in German and Afrikaans, ensuring equitable classification across languages.
\end{itemize}

